    "narrative": "The objective for Ghost Ride the WHIP today centers on capitalizing on the speed-heavy profiles in our lineup to chip away at our league-wide SB deficit. **Corbin Carroll** (72.47) is our unequivocal anchor, as his combination of the #2 spot and a favorable matchup against Gabriel Hughes makes him the premier start of the slate. He is joined by **Tyler Soderstrom** (70.68), who is benefitting from a significant park factor boost and a plus matchup against Freddy Peralta. While **Mickey Moniak** (61.62) and **Isaac Paredes** (60.10) both cleared the 60-point threshold, they represent the floor of our primary starts; **Mickey Moniak** in particular draws an intriguing platoon edge that elevates his ceiling against Michael Soroka despite the presence of a tough arm.\n\nDecisions in the middle of the roster required careful navigation of the constraints imposed by our limited game caps. **Brice Turang** (58.95) narrowly edged out a higher floor spot due to his high-leverage batting position at #2, even though Casey Mize presents a moderate challenge. **Gabriel Moreno** (57.23) and **Max Muncy** (56.82) occupy the marginal tier, but they remain locked in given the scarcity of depth on our bench. The most difficult personnel decision was navigating the potential output of **Austin Riley** (48.33), whose score is suppressed by a low lineup position and the looming 31% rain risk against Christian Scott. With **James Wood** and **Trevor Story** officially ruled out due to injury, and **Jose Caballero** and **Josh Naylor** inactive today, our bench options\u2014which include high-upside prospects like **Travis Bazzana**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte**, alongside veterans like **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Zach McKinstry**\u2014lack the immediate matchup utility to supplant our current starters. We will monitor the weather in the **Austin Riley** game closely, but for now, the roster remains set to maximize plate appearances.",
